━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ GrowRegion is Tuple

` A region of a growing table's storage: the slot of the directory it fills, the bytes a row
` takes in it and their alignment, and the name TypeScript's panics give it.

+ column U32
+ stride U32
+ alignment U32
+ name String

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ResolvedSpan is Tuple

` Where the indices an index span reads lie, once checked, and the first of them.

+ data Operand
+ offset Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ BuilderState is Tuple

` What an index span reads of an arena's builder: the identity of its storage, how many items
` it holds, its mutation generation, and its arena's owner and incarnation.

+ identity Operand
+ size Operand
+ mutation Operand
+ owner Operand
+ incarnation Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ TableBounds is Tuple

` Where a range of a table, or of a view of one, starts and how many rows or items it spans,
` from the range made forward.

+ start Operand
+ length Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Tables is facet of FunctionEmitter

────────────────────
_ proven-table U32
    - id SyntaxId

|? facts.plan-of(unit.reading, id) != .plan-table || constant == no-fact
    U32.max
|? ((bits /and/ 4294967295) as U32) as TableOp != TableOp.proven-row
    U32.max
??
    proven-loop((bits /rshift/ 32) as SyntaxId)

.. constant = facts.constant-of(unit.reading, id)
.. bits = facts.constants[constant].bits

────────────────────
_ do proven-field Operand
    - id SyntaxId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - column U32
    - index Operand
    - field LayoutField

. found = proven-read(loop, column)
if found != U32.max
    = proven-reads[found].value
. read = take
    - item-cell(id, hoisted-column(loop, column), index, field.layout)
    - LayoutField(0, field.layout, field.type)
    - id
proven-reads += ProvenRead(loop, column, ir.current, read, field.type)
= read

────────────────────
_ do hoisted-column Operand
    - loop SyntaxId
    - column U32

for held in proven-columns
    if held.loop == loop && held.column == column
        = load-local(held.local, loop)
. local = ir.add-local(pointer-layout)
proven-columns += ProvenColumn(loop, column, local)
= load-local(local, loop)

────────────────────
+ do emit-table-constructor
    - declared SyntaxId
    - kind DeclKind

` A table's constructor the compiler generates, as TypeScript generates it: one of a size
` makes storage for that many rows, each zero, and one of a size and a filler then fills each
` row in turn with what the filler answers for its index, scattering it into the columns. One
` of an arena, and of a capacity, makes a table that grows in the arena.
if is-index-span-constructor-kind(kind)
    emit-span-constructor(declared, kind)
    =
. type = instances.rows[unit.instance].self-type
. row = table-row-type(type)
. row-kind = if row != no-type then types.intrinsic-of(row) else IntrinsicKind.none
if row-kind != .struct && row-kind != .union
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
. grows = kind == .table-arena-constructor-decl || kind == .table-capacity-constructor-decl
if kind != .table-size-constructor-decl && kind != .table-filler-constructor-decl && !grows
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
. layout = layout-of(type, declared)
. row-layout = layout-of(row, declared)
. signature = instances.signatures[unit.instance]
for position in 0 .. < signature.args.count
    ir.add-argument(layout-of(instances.argument-type(unit.instance, position), declared))
if !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout) || !tables.layouts.is-struct(row-layout)
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
returns-type = type
ir.returns = layout
if row-kind == .union
    emit-union-constructor(declared, kind, layout, row, row-layout)
    =
if grows
    . needed = if kind == .table-capacity-constructor-decl then second else integer(.machine-u64, 0)
        .. second = make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
    grown-table(declared, layout, row, row-layout, needed)
    =
. size = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. columns = fixed-columns(declared, row-layout, size)
if kind == .table-filler-constructor-decl
    fill-table(declared, row, row-layout, columns, size, make-operand(.operand-argument, 1))
. zero = integer(.machine-u64, 0)
return-table(declared, layout, columns, size, TableMeta(zero, zero, zero, zero, zero))

────────────────────
_ do emit-union-constructor
    - declared SyntaxId
    - kind DeclKind
    - layout LayoutId
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId

` A table of union rows, made as TypeScript makes it: one that does not grow has its columns,
` then each row set to the first case's first value, or filled in turn with what the filler
` answers; one that grows is made as a table of structs is, with a column for each region.
. place = tables.unions.of(row)
if place == U32.max
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
if kind == .table-arena-constructor-decl || kind == .table-capacity-constructor-decl
    . needed = if kind == .table-capacity-constructor-decl then second else integer(.machine-u64, 0)
        .. second = make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
    grown-table(declared, layout, row, row-layout, needed)
    =
if kind != .table-size-constructor-decl && kind != .table-filler-constructor-decl
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
. size = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. columns = union-columns(declared, place, size)
if kind == .table-filler-constructor-decl
    fill-table(declared, row, row-layout, columns, size, make-operand(.operand-argument, 1))
else
    clear-union-rows(declared, place, columns, size)
. zero = integer(.machine-u64, 0)
return-table(declared, layout, columns, size, TableMeta(zero, zero, zero, zero, zero))

────────────────────
_ do union-columns Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - size Operand

` The storage of a table of union rows that does not grow, as TypeScript makes it: the rows
` are checked to keep their outside bytes within what a handle reaches, then a directory, the
` tags, a column for each shared field, the inline bytes, the handles and the outside bytes.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
if union.external-stride != 0
    . most = integer(.machine-u64, (4294967295 / (union.external-stride as U64)))
    fail-if
        - site
        - compare(site, .compare-greater, size, most)
        - "Table union external storage exceeds the U32 handle limit"
. directory = table-buffer(site, managed-layout, integer(.machine-u64, union.columns))
store(directory, 0, table-buffer(site, u8-layout, size), false, site)
. first = types.cases-of(union.union)[0].type
. first-layout = layout-of(first, site)
for position in 0 .. < union.commons.count
    . common = tables.unions.fields[union.commons.start + position]
    . field = tables.layouts.field(first-layout, common.slot)
    store(directory, common.column * 8, table-buffer(site, field.layout, size), false, site)
if union.inline-column != U32.max
    . bytes = arithmetic
        - site
        - .arithmetic-multiply
        - size
        - integer(.machine-u64, union.inline-stride)
        - u64-layout
    store(directory, union.inline-column * 8, table-buffer(site, u8-layout, bytes), false, site)
if union.handle-column != U32.max
    store(directory, union.handle-column * 8, table-buffer(site, u32-layout, size), false, site)
if union.external-column != U32.max
    . bytes = arithmetic
        - site
        - .arithmetic-multiply
        - size
        - integer(.machine-u64, union.external-stride)
        - u64-layout
    store(directory, union.external-column * 8, table-buffer(site, u8-layout, bytes), false, site)
= directory

────────────────────
_ do clear-union-rows
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - columns Operand
    - size Operand

` Sets each row of a new table of unions, from the first, to the first case's first value, as
` TypeScript sets them to the union's default.
. first = types.cases-of(tables.unions.layouts[place].union)[0].type
. first-layout = layout-of(first, site)
if tables.writes-constructor(first)
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    =
. counting = open-pass(site, size)
. index = counting.index
. empty = make-fields(first, first-layout, RowRange'ArgumentFill(), given.length, 0, site)
scatter-union-case(site, place, 0, columns, index, empty, no-meta(), false, false)
close-pass(site, counting)

────────────────────
+ do union-cell Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand
    - field UnionField
    - item LayoutId
    - handle Operand

` Where a row of a table of unions keeps a field of a case: in its shared field's column, among
` the row's inline bytes, or among the outside bytes its handle leads to.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
if field.region == .region-common
    = table-cell(site, columns, index, field.column, item)
if field.region == .region-inline
    . inline = load(columns, union.inline-column * 8, pointer-layout, site)
    . row = arithmetic
        - site
        - .arithmetic-multiply
        - index
        - integer(.machine-u64, union.inline-stride)
        - u64-layout
    = moved-bytes
        - site
        - inline
        - arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, row, integer(.machine-u64, field.offset), u64-layout)
. outside = load(columns, union.external-column * 8, pointer-layout, site)
. start = arithmetic
    - site
    - .arithmetic-subtract
    - num-cast(site, handle, u32-layout, u64-layout)
    - integer(.machine-u64, 1)
    - u64-layout
= moved-bytes
    - site
    - outside
    - arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, start, integer(.machine-u64, field.offset), u64-layout)

────────────────────
+ do union-handle Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand

` The handle a row of a table of unions keeps for its outside bytes.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
= load(table-cell(site, columns, index, union.handle-column, u32-layout), 0, u32-layout, site)

────────────────────
_ do scatter-union-case
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - case-index U32
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand
    - payload Operand
    - meta TableMeta
    - checked Bool
    - replacing Bool

` Stores a row of one case in a table of unions, as TypeScript scatters it: the row's handle
` first, where the table keeps one, then each field of the case in the order it declares them,
` and the tag last. `checked` says the table's metadata is given: where the table grows, the
` handle is to the row's outside bytes in its spill, the columns are read again from its header,
` and the fields are stored plainly. `replacing` says the row is one the table holds already,
` which keeps its handle when the case has no outside bytes, and keeps the bytes its handle
` leads to when it has.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
. held = tables.unions.cases[union.cases.start + case-index]
. case-layout = layout-of(held.type, site)
. handle = integer(.machine-u32, 0)
if union.handle-column != U32.max
    . cell = table-cell(site, columns, index, union.handle-column, u32-layout)
    if held.external-size != 0
        handle = case-handle(site, place, index, cell, meta, checked, replacing)
    if held.external-size != 0 || !replacing
        store(cell, 0, handle, false, site)
. into = if checked then growing-columns(site, columns, meta) else columns
for position in 0 .. < held.fields.count
    . field = tables.unions.fields[held.fields.start + position]
    . stored = tables.layouts.field(case-layout, field.slot)
    . cell = union-cell(site, place, into, index, field, stored.layout, handle)
    if checked
        store-row-cell(site, cell, stored.layout, take(payload, stored, site), meta)
    else
        store-cell(site, cell, stored.layout, take(payload, stored, site))
store(table-cell(site, into, index, 0, u8-layout), 0, integer(.machine-u8, case-index), false, site)

────────────────────
_ do case-handle Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - index Operand
    - cell Operand
    - meta TableMeta
    - checked Bool
    - replacing Bool

` The handle of the outside bytes of a row of a case: one past the row's place among them where
` the table does not grow, and its handle in the spill where it grows.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
if !checked
    = fixed-handle(site, union, index)
. spilling = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(view-grows(site, meta), spilling, fixed)
ir.start-block(spilling)
. spilled = spill-handle(site, place, cell, meta, replacing)
. from-spilling = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
. placed = fixed-handle(site, union, index)
. from-fixed = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(u32-layout, spilled, from-spilling, placed, from-fixed)

────────────────────
_ do spill-handle Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - cell Operand
    - meta TableMeta
    - replacing Bool

` The handle of a row's outside bytes in the spill of a table that grows. Every block of the
` spill suits every case, so a row the table holds already keeps the block its handle leads to,
` where it has one; any other row is given a block reserved in the spill.
if !replacing
    = reserved-handle(site, place, meta)
. kept = load(cell, 0, u32-layout, site)
. from-kept = ir.current
. reserving = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-not-equal, kept, integer(.machine-u32, 0)), joined, reserving)
ir.start-block(reserving)
. reserved = reserved-handle(site, place, meta)
. from-reserving = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(u32-layout, kept, from-kept, reserved, from-reserving)

────────────────────
_ do reserved-handle Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - meta TableMeta

` The handle of a block newly reserved in the spill of a table of unions that grows: one past it.
= arithmetic
    - site
    - .arithmetic-add
    - num-cast(site, reserve-spill(site, place, meta), u64-layout, u32-layout)
    - integer(.machine-u32, 1)
    - u32-layout

────────────────────
_ do fixed-handle Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - union UnionLayout
    - index Operand

` The handle of a row's outside bytes in a table that does not grow: one past its place.
. offset = arithmetic
    - site
    - .arithmetic-multiply
    - index
    - integer(.machine-u64, union.external-stride)
    - u64-layout
= arithmetic
    - site
    - .arithmetic-add
    - num-cast(site, offset, u64-layout, u32-layout)
    - integer(.machine-u32, 1)
    - u32-layout

────────────────────
_ do reserve-spill Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - meta TableMeta

` Reserves a block of outside bytes in the spill of a table of unions that grows: the table is
` checked as a view, and the spill's use checked to stay within what a U32 handle reaches, the
` spill grown where it is full, and its use counted on. Each block is as wide and as aligned as
` the union's widest outside bytes need, as the rows of a table that does not grow keep them,
` so a block suits whichever case its row holds next. The spill is grown by the function the
` tables declared to, as `grow-outside` says, and where they declared none, here. The answer is
` where the bytes start.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
. limit = 4294967295u64
. text = "Table union spill exceeds the U32 handle limit"
validate-table(site, meta, "Table union spill", false)
. used = header-word(site, meta.header, 6)
. stride = union.external-stride as U64
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-greater, used, integer(.machine-u64, limit - stride)), text)
. needed = arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, used, integer(.machine-u64, stride), u64-layout)
. capacity = header-word(site, meta.header, 7)
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-greater, needed, capacity), growing, joined)
ir.start-block(growing)
. helper = tables.growth-of(union.union, 1)
if cold || helper == no-function
    grow-spill(site, union, meta, used, capacity, needed)
else
    grow-outside(site, helper, meta, used, capacity, needed)
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
put-header(site, meta.header, 6, needed)
= used

────────────────────
+ do grow-spill
    - site SyntaxId
    - union UnionLayout
    - meta TableMeta
    - used Operand
    - capacity Operand
    - needed Operand

` Grows the spill of a table of unions, as TypeScript's generated growth does: the capacity
` doubles as a table's of one-byte rows does, to at least 64 bytes and within what a U32
` handle reaches; the bytes are reserved in the arena and those used copied over, and the
` directory's slot of the outside bytes and the header are given the new spill.
. text = "Table union spill exceeds the U32 handle limit"
. chosen = next-capacity(site, capacity, needed, 8, "Table capacity overflow")
. least = integer(.machine-u64, 64)
. next = at-least(site, chosen, least)
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-greater, next, integer(.machine-u64, 4294967295)), text)
. owner = num-cast(site, meta.owner, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. replacement = arena-reserve(site, owner, meta.incarnation, next, union.external-alignment, false)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-equal, replacement, integer(.machine-pointer, 0))
    - "Arena allocation failed while growing Table union spill"
. copying = ir.reserve-block()
. copied = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-greater, used, integer(.machine-u64, 0)), copying, copied)
ir.start-block(copying)
. prior = num-cast(site, header-word(site, meta.header, 5), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
copy-bytes(site, replacement, prior, used)
jump(copied)
ir.start-block(copied)
. columns = num-cast(site, header-word(site, meta.header, 0), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
store(columns, union.external-column * 8, replacement, false, site)
put-header(site, meta.header, 5, num-cast(site, replacement, pointer-layout, u64-layout))
put-header(site, meta.header, 7, next)

────────────────────
_ do at-least Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - value Operand
    - least Operand

` A count raised to a least one where it is less.
. raising = ir.reserve-block()
. keeping = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-less, value, least), raising, keeping)
ir.start-block(raising)
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(keeping)
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(u64-layout, least, raising, value, keeping)

────────────────────
+ do no-meta TableMeta

` The metadata of a table that does not grow.
. zero = integer(.machine-u64, 0)
= TableMeta(zero, zero, zero, zero, zero)

────────────────────
_ do growing-columns Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - columns Operand
    - meta TableMeta

` A table's columns read again from its header where it grows, as TypeScript reads them after
` a store that may grow it.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(view-grows(site, meta), growing, fixed)
ir.start-block(growing)
. held = num-cast(site, header-word(site, meta.header, 0), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. from-growing = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
. from-fixed = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(pointer-layout, held, from-growing, columns, from-fixed)

────────────────────
_ do scatter-union
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand
    - value Operand
    - meta TableMeta
    - checked Bool
    - replacing Bool

` Stores a union in a row of a table of unions: the case it holds, each case tested in turn.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
. union-layout = layout-of(union.union, site)
. tag = load(value, 0, u8-layout, site)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
for position in 0 .. < union.cases.count
    . storing = ir.reserve-block()
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(site, .compare-equal, tag, integer(.machine-u8, position)), storing, next)
    ir.start-block(storing)
    scatter-union-case
        - site
        - place
        - position
        - columns
        - index
        - take(value, tables.layouts.case-field(union-layout, position), site)
        - meta
        - checked
        - replacing
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
_ do gather-union Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand

` A row of a table of unions read as the union, as TypeScript gathers it: the case the tag
` names, built from its fields; a tag that names no case gives the first case's first value.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
. union-layout = layout-of(union.union, site)
. made = frame(union-layout)
. tag = load(table-cell(site, columns, index, 0, u8-layout), 0, u8-layout, site)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
for position in 0 .. < union.cases.count
    . reading = ir.reserve-block()
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(site, .compare-equal, tag, integer(.machine-u8, position)), reading, next)
    ir.start-block(reading)
    . read = gather-union-case(site, place, position, columns, index)
    copy(made, make-union(site, union.union, position, read).operand, union-layout, false, site)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
. first = types.cases-of(union.union)[0].type
. first-layout = layout-of(first, site)
if tables.writes-constructor(first)
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = Typed(columns, no-type)
. empty = make-fields(first, first-layout, RowRange'ArgumentFill(), given.length, 0, site)
copy(made, make-union(site, union.union, 0, Typed(empty, first)).operand, union-layout, false, site)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
= Typed(made, union.union)

────────────────────
+ do gather-union-case Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - case-index U32
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand

` A row of one case of a table of unions read as the case: each field from where it is kept.
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
. held = tables.unions.cases[union.cases.start + case-index]
. case-layout = layout-of(held.type, site)
. handle = if union.handle-column != U32.max then union-handle(site, place, columns, index) else integer(.machine-u32, 0)
. made = frame(case-layout)
for position in 0 .. < held.fields.count
    . field = tables.unions.fields[held.fields.start + position]
    . stored = tables.layouts.field(case-layout, field.slot)
    . cell = union-cell(site, place, columns, index, field, stored.layout, handle)
    put(made, stored, take(cell, LayoutField(0, stored.layout, stored.type), site), site)
= Typed(made, held.type)

────────────────────
_ do emit-span-constructor
    - declared SyntaxId
    - kind DeclKind

` The constructor the compiler generates of an index span, as TypeScript generates it: the
` span of the whole of its source, or of the range it is given, made forward.
. type = instances.rows[unit.instance].self-type
. layout = layout-of(type, declared)
. signature = instances.signatures[unit.instance]
for position in 0 .. < signature.args.count
    ir.add-argument(layout-of(instances.argument-type(unit.instance, position), declared))
if !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
returns-type = type
ir.returns = layout
. ranged = kind == .index-span-range-constructor-decl
. range = if ranged then make-operand(.operand-argument, 1) else make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. range-type = if ranged then instances.argument-type(unit.instance, 1) else no-type
. in-place = tables.layouts.is-large(layout)
. made = if in-place then make-operand(.operand-result, 0) else frame(layout)
span-into
    - declared
    - made
    - type
    - layout
    - make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
    - instances.argument-type(unit.instance, 0)
    - range
    - range-type
if in-place
    return-nothing()
else
    return-value(made, declared)

────────────────────
_ do span-into
    - site SyntaxId
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId
    - layout LayoutId
    - source Operand
    - source-type TypeId
    - range Operand
    - range-type TypeId

` An index span made of its source, as TypeScript makes one: of an array, where its items lie,
` from the first the range spans, or the first, for as many as the range spans, or the array
` holds; of an arena's builder, the identity of the builder's storage in place of where the
` items lie, with its mutation generation and its arena's owner, incarnation and generation,
` which say whether the span can still be read. A range is made forward where the
` constructor runs.
. item = viewed-item(type)
. item-layout = layout-of(item, site)
. source-layout = layout-of(source-type, site)
if viewed-item(source-type) != item
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    =
. width = integer(.machine-u64, tables.layouts.rows[item-layout].size)
. zero = integer(.machine-u64, 0)
. words [Operand]
if is-array-type(source-type)
    . data = word-at(site, source, source-layout, 0)
    . length = word-at(site, source, source-layout, 1)
    . bounds = given-bounds(site, range, range-type, length)
    words = [data, zero, bounds.start, bounds.length, width, zero, zero, zero, zero]
else if intrinsic(source-type) == .array-builder
    . state = builder-state(site, source, source-layout)
    . bounds = given-bounds(site, range, range-type, state.size)
    . mark = pending.length
    pending += num-cast(site, state.owner, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
    pending += state.incarnation
    . generation = call-runtime(.runtime-arena-generation, site, mark, u64-layout)
    words = [zero, state.identity, bounds.start, bounds.length, width, state.mutation, state.owner, state.incarnation, generation]
else
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    =
for position in 0 .. < words.length
    put-word(site, made, layout, position as U32, words[position], u64-layout)

────────────────────
_ do builder-state BuilderState
    - site SyntaxId
    - builder Operand
    - layout LayoutId

` What an index span reads of an arena's builder, as TypeScript reads it: the builder holds
` the header its copies share, which is the identity of its storage and holds the storage, its
` capacity, the size and the mutation generation; the builder's context is its arena.
. identity = word-at(site, builder, layout, 0)
. held = num-cast(site, identity, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. size = load(held, 16, u64-layout, site)
. mutation = load(held, 24, u64-layout, site)
. arena-layout = tables.layouts.field(layout, 1).layout
. arena = part(builder, layout, 1, site)
= BuilderState
    - identity
    - size
    - mutation
    - word-at(site, arena.operand, arena-layout, 0)
    - word-at(site, arena.operand, arena-layout, 1)

────────────────────
_ do given-bounds TableBounds
    - site SyntaxId
    - range Operand
    - range-type TypeId
    - length Operand

` The indices an index span's constructor spans: those its range spans, made forward by the
` call recorded for the constructor, or else every one of the source's.
if range-type == no-type
    = TableBounds(integer(.machine-u64, 0), length)
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fact = tables.loose-call(unit.instance, 0)
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].callee == no-instance || uncallable
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    = TableBounds(none, none)
.. uncallable = !is-callable(facts.calls[fact].callee)
. mark = pending.length
pending += range
. forward = call-method(facts.calls[fact].callee, site, mark)
= checked-bounds(site, forward.operand, forward.type, length)

────────────────────
_ do checked-bounds TableBounds
    - site SyntaxId
    - forward Operand
    - forward-type TypeId
    - length Operand

` The indices a range made forward spans of an index span's, as TypeScript checks them: the
` range steps by one, and starts and ends inside the length, its end not before its start.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. layout = layout-of(forward-type, site)
. start = range-index(site, forward, forward-type, layout, "start")
. end = range-index(site, forward, forward-type, layout, "end")
. increment = range-index(site, forward, forward-type, layout, "increment")
. outside = "IndexSpan range is out of bounds"
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-not-equal, increment.operand, integer(.machine-u64, 1))
    - "IndexSpan requires a contiguous range"
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-greater, start.operand, length), outside)
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-greater, end.operand, length), outside)
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-less, end.operand, start.operand), outside)
= TableBounds(start.operand, arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-subtract, end.operand, start.operand, u64-layout))

────────────────────
+ do resolve-span ResolvedSpan
    - site SyntaxId
    - span Operand
    - layout LayoutId

` Where the indices an index span reads lie, as TypeScript finds them: an array's, where the
` span holds them; a builder's, once the span is checked to read it still, as its storage
` holds them now. The arena must not be reset, nor rewound past the storage, and the builder
` neither changed nor shrunk past the span since the span was made.
. source = word-at(site, span, layout, 0)
. identity = word-at(site, span, layout, 1)
. offset = word-at(site, span, layout, 2)
. length = word-at(site, span, layout, 3)
. built = ir.reserve-block()
. plain = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-not-equal, identity, integer(.machine-u64, 0)), built, plain)
ir.start-block(built)
. owner = num-cast(site, word-at(site, span, layout, 6), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. incarnation = word-at(site, span, layout, 7)
. mark = pending.length
pending += owner
pending += incarnation
. current = call-runtime(.runtime-arena-generation, site, mark, u64-layout)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-not-equal, current, word-at(site, span, layout, 8))
    - "IndexSpan is stale after Arena reset"
. rewound = "IndexSpan was invalidated by Arena rewind"
. held = num-cast(site, identity, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare
        - site
        - .compare-equal
        - arena-owns(site, owner, incarnation, held)
        - integer(.machine-u8, 0)
    - rewound
fail-if
    - site
    - compare
        - site
        - .compare-not-equal
        - load(held, 24, u64-layout, site)
        - word-at(site, span, layout, 5)
    - "IndexSpan was invalidated by ArrayBuilder mutation"
. size = load(held, 16, u64-layout, site)
. shrunk = "IndexSpan was invalidated by ArrayBuilder shrink"
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-greater, offset, size), shrunk)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare
        - site
        - .compare-greater
        - length
        - arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-subtract, size, offset, u64-layout)
    - shrunk
. data = load(held, 0, u64-layout, site)
. owning = ir.reserve-block()
. owned = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-not-equal, size, integer(.machine-u64, 0)), owning, owned)
ir.start-block(owning)
. pointer = num-cast(site, data, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare
        - site
        - .compare-equal
        - arena-owns(site, owner, incarnation, pointer)
        - integer(.machine-u8, 0)
    - rewound
jump(owned)
ir.start-block(owned)
. from-built = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(plain)
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= ResolvedSpan(phi(u64-layout, data, from-built, source, plain), offset)

────────────────────
_ do arena-owns Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - owner Operand
    - incarnation Operand
    - address Operand

` Whether an arena holds an address in what it has reserved.
. mark = pending.length
pending += owner
pending += incarnation
pending += address
= call-runtime(.runtime-arena-owns, site, mark, u8-layout)

────────────────────
+ do span-item Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - resolved ResolvedSpan
    - position Operand
    - item LayoutId

` The index an index span reads at a position, where its indices lie.
. data = num-cast(site, resolved.data, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. moved = arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, resolved.offset, position, u64-layout)
= load(item-cell(site, data, moved, item), 0, item, site)

────────────────────
+ do selected-index Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - resolved ResolvedSpan
    - position Operand
    - item TypeId
    - item-layout LayoutId

` The index of a table's row a selection reads at a position, as TypeScript reads it: one of
` a signed type below zero is out of bounds.
. value = span-item(site, resolved, position, item-layout)
if is-signed-item(item)
    fail-if
        - site
        - compare(site, .compare-less, value, integer(tables.layouts.rows[item-layout].kind, 0))
        - "TableSelection index is out of bounds"
= num-cast(site, value, item-layout, u64-layout)

────────────────────
_ is-signed-item Bool
    - item TypeId

` Whether the indices of a span are of a signed type.
kind == .int8 || kind == .int16 || kind == .int32 || kind == .int64

.. kind = types.intrinsic-of(item)

────────────────────
_ do return-table
    - site SyntaxId
    - layout LayoutId
    - columns Operand
    - size Operand
    - meta TableMeta

` Answers a table made by its constructor: its columns, its size, and its header, owner,
` incarnation and generation, each zero for a table that does not grow.
. in-place = tables.layouts.is-large(layout)
. made = if in-place then make-operand(.operand-result, 0) else frame(layout)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 0), columns, site)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 1), size, site)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 2), meta.header, site)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 3), meta.owner, site)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 4), meta.incarnation, site)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 5), meta.generation, site)
if in-place
    return-nothing()
else
    return-value(made, site)

────────────────────
_ do grown-table
    - site SyntaxId
    - layout LayoutId
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - needed Operand

` The body of the constructor of a table that grows in an arena, as TypeScript writes it: the
` header is reserved in the arena, zeroed, then the directory of its columns, one slot for each
` column; the arena's generation is read, the header given the directory, and room reserved for
` the rows the capacity asks for. The table holds the directory, a size of zero, the header,
` and the arena's owner, incarnation and generation.
. arena-type = instances.argument-type(unit.instance, 0)
. arena = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. arena-layout = layout-of(arena-type, site)
. owner = part(arena, arena-layout, 0, site)
. incarnation = part(arena, arena-layout, 1, site)
. header = arena-reserve(site, owner.operand, incarnation.operand, integer(.machine-u64, 64), 8, true)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-equal, header, integer(.machine-pointer, 0))
    - "Arena allocation failed while creating Table header"
. count = directory-slots(row, row-layout)
. slots U64 = if count != 0 then count as U64 else 1
. directory = arena-reserve(site, owner.operand, incarnation.operand, integer(.machine-u64, slots * 8), 8, true)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-equal, directory, integer(.machine-pointer, 0))
    - "Arena allocation failed while creating Table directory"
. mark = pending.length
pending += owner.operand
pending += incarnation.operand
. generation = call-runtime(.runtime-arena-generation, site, mark, u64-layout)
store(header, 0, directory, false, site)
for position in 1 .. < 8u32
    store(header, position * 8, integer(.machine-u64, 0), false, site)
. held = num-cast(site, header, pointer-layout, u64-layout)
. handle = word-at(site, arena, arena-layout, 0)
reserve-rows
    - site
    - row
    - row-layout
    - TableMeta(held, handle, incarnation.operand, generation, integer(.machine-u64, 0))
    - needed
. columns = num-cast(site, directory, pointer-layout, managed-layout)
return-table
    - site
    - layout
    - columns
    - integer(.machine-u64, 0)
    - TableMeta(held, handle, incarnation.operand, generation, integer(.machine-u64, 0))

────────────────────
_ do arena-reserve Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - owner Operand
    - incarnation Operand
    - bytes Operand
    - alignment U64
    - zeroed Bool

` Reserves bytes in an arena, zeroed or not, as TypeScript reserves a table's storage: the
` address reserved, or null where the arena is gone or out of room.
. mark = pending.length
pending += owner
pending += incarnation
pending += bytes
pending += integer(.machine-u64, alignment)
pending += integer(.machine-u8, if zeroed then 1 else 0)
= call-runtime(.runtime-arena-reserve, site, mark, pointer-layout)

────────────────────
_ do reserve-rows
    - site SyntaxId
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta
    - needed Operand

` Makes room in a table that grows for as many rows as are needed, where its capacity is less:
` by the function the tables declared to grow such rows, as `grow-outside` says, and where
` they declared none, here.
. header = num-cast(site, meta.header, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. current = load(header, 16, u64-layout, site)
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-greater, needed, current), growing, joined)
ir.start-block(growing)
. helper = tables.growth-of(row, 0)
if cold || helper == no-function
    grow-rows(site, row, row-layout, meta, current, needed)
else
    grow-outside(site, helper, meta, current, needed, make-operand(.operand-void, 0))
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)

────────────────────
+ do grow-rows
    - site SyntaxId
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta
    - current Operand
    - needed Operand

` Grows a table's storage in its arena, as TypeScript's generated growth does: the capacity
` is chosen, each region reserved again in turn with its rows copied over, then a new
` directory reserved and given each region, and the slot of a union's outside bytes as it
` was; the header is given the directory and the capacity. What was reserved before stays in
` the arena.
. regions = grow-regions(site, row, row-layout)
. width U64
for region in regions
    width += region.stride as U64
if width == 0
    width = 1
. first U64 = if width == 1 then 8 else if width <= 1024 then 4 else 1
. next = next-capacity(site, current, needed, first, "Table capacity overflow")
. header = num-cast(site, meta.header, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. owner = num-cast(site, meta.owner, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. columns = num-cast(site, load(header, 0, u64-layout, site), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. live = load(header, 8, u64-layout, site)
. replacements [Operand]
for region in regions
    . context = "Table ${region.name}"
    . bytes = checked-bytes(site, next, region.stride, context)
    . replacement = arena-reserve(site, owner, meta.incarnation, bytes, region.alignment, false)
    fail-if
        - site
        - compare(site, .compare-equal, replacement, integer(.machine-pointer, 0))
        - "Arena allocation failed while growing Table"
    . prior = load(columns, region.column * 8, pointer-layout, site)
    . copied = checked-bytes(site, live, region.stride, context)
    . copying = ir.reserve-block()
    . joined = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(site, .compare-greater, copied, integer(.machine-u64, 0)), copying, joined)
    ir.start-block(copying)
    copy-bytes(site, replacement, prior, copied)
    jump(joined)
    ir.start-block(joined)
    replacements += replacement
. count = directory-slots(row, row-layout)
. slots U64 = if count != 0 then count as U64 else 1
. directory = arena-reserve
    - site
    - owner
    - meta.incarnation
    - integer(.machine-u64, slots * 8)
    - 8
    - true
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-equal, directory, integer(.machine-pointer, 0))
    - "Arena allocation failed while growing Table directory"
for slot in 0 .. < count
    . kept = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
    . found = false
    for position in 0 .. < regions.length
        if regions[position].column == slot
            kept = replacements[position]
            found = true
    if !found
        kept = load(columns, slot * 8, pointer-layout, site)
    store(directory, slot * 8, kept, false, site)
store(header, 0, directory, false, site)
store(header, 16, next, false, site)

────────────────────
_ do grow-regions [GrowRegion]
    - site SyntaxId
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId

` The regions of a growing table's storage, as TypeScript lists them: a column for each field
` of a struct row; for a union row the tag, each shared field, the inline bytes and the
` handles of the outside bytes.
. regions [GrowRegion]
. place = if types.intrinsic-of(row) == .union then tables.unions.of(row) else U32.max
if place == U32.max
    for position in 0 .. < tables.layouts.rows[row-layout].fields.count
        . item = tables.layouts.rows[tables.layouts.field(row-layout, position).layout]
        regions += GrowRegion(position, item.size, item.alignment, region-name(row, position))
    = regions
. union = tables.unions.layouts[place]
regions += GrowRegion(0, 1, 1, "tag")
. first = types.cases-of(row)[0].type
. first-layout = layout-of(first, site)
for position in 0 .. < union.commons.count
    . common = tables.unions.fields[union.commons.start + position]
    . item = tables.layouts.rows[tables.layouts.field(first-layout, common.slot).layout]
    regions += GrowRegion
        - common.column
        - item.size
        - item.alignment
        - "common ${region-name(first, common.slot)}"
if union.inline-column != U32.max
    regions += GrowRegion
        - union.inline-column
        - union.inline-stride
        - union.inline-alignment
        - "inline"
if union.handle-column != U32.max
    regions += GrowRegion(union.handle-column, 4, 4, "spill-handles")
= regions

────────────────────
_ directory-slots U32
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId

` How many slots the directory of a table's columns has: one for each field of a struct row,
` and for a union row one for each column and one for its outside bytes.
|? types.intrinsic-of(row) == .union && tables.unions.of(row) != U32.max
    tables.unions.layouts[tables.unions.of(row)].columns
??
    tables.layouts.rows[row-layout].fields.count

────────────────────
_ do region-name String
    - row TypeId
    - position U32

` The name of a field of a row at its place in the row's layout, as TypeScript names the
` region of a table's storage that holds its column.
for property in types.properties-of(row)
    if property.slot == position
        = property.name.text
= "field $position"

────────────────────
_ do checked-bytes Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - count Operand
    - stride U64
    - context String

` How many bytes a count of items of a size takes, checked first not to overflow.
. most = integer(.machine-u64, U64.max / stride)
fail-if(site, compare(site, .compare-greater, count, most), "$context capacity overflow")
= arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-multiply, count, integer(.machine-u64, stride), u64-layout)

────────────────────
_ do next-capacity Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - current Operand
    - needed Operand
    - first U64
    - overflow String

` The capacity a table or an arena's builder grows to, as TypeScript chooses it: from none, the
` first capacity; under 1024, twice as many; and else half as many again, with the panic of an
` overflow. It is never less than is needed.
. most = integer(.machine-u64, U64.max)
. empty = ir.reserve-block()
. held = ir.reserve-block()
. small = ir.reserve-block()
. large = ir.reserve-block()
. grew = ir.reserve-block()
. chosen = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-equal, current, integer(.machine-u64, 0)), empty, held)
ir.start-block(empty)
jump(chosen)
ir.start-block(held)
branch(compare(site, .compare-less, current, integer(.machine-u64, 1024)), small, large)
ir.start-block(small)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-greater, current, integer(.machine-u64, U64.max / 2))
    - overflow
. doubled = arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-multiply, current, integer(.machine-u64, 2), u64-layout)
. from-small = ir.current
jump(grew)
ir.start-block(large)
. half = arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-divide, current, integer(.machine-u64, 2), u64-layout)
fail-if
    - site
    - compare
        - site
        - .compare-greater
        - current
        - arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-subtract, most, half, u64-layout)
    - overflow
. grown = arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, current, half, u64-layout)
. from-large = ir.current
jump(grew)
ir.start-block(grew)
. later = phi(u64-layout, doubled, from-small, grown, from-large)
. from-grew = ir.current
jump(chosen)
ir.start-block(chosen)
. candidate = phi(u64-layout, integer(.machine-u64, first), empty, later, from-grew)
. short = ir.reserve-block()
. enough = ir.reserve-block()
. settled = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-less, candidate, needed), short, enough)
ir.start-block(short)
jump(settled)
ir.start-block(enough)
jump(settled)
ir.start-block(settled)
= phi(u64-layout, needed, short, candidate, enough)

────────────────────
_ do copy-bytes
    - site SyntaxId
    - target Operand
    - source Operand
    - count Operand

` Copies bytes from one place to another, as TypeScript copies a table's rows when it grows: a
` word at a time while a whole word is left, then a byte at a time.
. cursor = ir.add-local(u64-layout)
store-local(cursor, integer(.machine-u64, 0), site)
copy-by(site, target, source, count, cursor, 8, u64-layout)
copy-by(site, target, source, count, cursor, 1, u8-layout)

────────────────────
_ do copy-by
    - site SyntaxId
    - target Operand
    - source Operand
    - count Operand
    - cursor LocalId
    - width U64
    - layout LayoutId

` Copies bytes a width at a time from the cursor on, while a whole width is left.
. testing = ir.reserve-block()
. copying = ir.reserve-block()
. copied = ir.reserve-block()
jump(testing)
ir.start-block(testing)
. end = arithmetic
    - site
    - .arithmetic-add
    - load-local(cursor, site)
    - integer(.machine-u64, width)
    - u64-layout
branch(compare(site, .compare-greater, end, count), copied, copying)
ir.start-block(copying)
. done = load-local(cursor, site)
. value = load(moved-bytes(site, source, done), 0, layout, site)
store(moved-bytes(site, target, done), 0, value, false, site)
store-local
    - cursor
    - arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, done, integer(.machine-u64, width), u64-layout)
    - site
jump(testing)
ir.start-block(copied)

────────────────────
+ table-row-type TypeId
    - table TypeId

` The type of a table's rows, or of the rows a view of one reads.
viewed-item(table)

────────────────────
_ do fixed-columns Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - size Operand

` The storage of a table that does not grow, as TypeScript makes it: a directory with a
` pointer to each field's column, and a buffer for each column. Where every field has the
` same type, which holds nothing the collector follows, the columns are parts of one buffer.
. fields = tables.layouts.rows[row-layout].fields
. count = fields.count
. directory = table-buffer(site, managed-layout, integer(.machine-u64, count))
if count == 0
    = directory
. first = tables.layouts.field(row-layout, 0)
. uniform = !tables.layouts.rows[first.layout].is-managed
for position in 1 .. < count
    if tables.layouts.field(row-layout, position).type != first.type
        uniform = false
if uniform
    . total = arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-multiply, size, integer(.machine-u64, count), u64-layout)
    . slab = table-buffer(site, first.layout, total)
    . width = tables.layouts.rows[first.layout].size as U64
    for position in 0 .. < count
        . start = integer(.machine-u64, 0)
        if position != 0
            start = arithmetic
                - site
                - .arithmetic-multiply
                - size
                - integer(.machine-u64, position)
                - u64-layout
        . bytes = arithmetic
            - site
            - .arithmetic-multiply
            - start
            - integer(.machine-u64, width)
            - u64-layout
        store(directory, position * 8, moved-bytes(site, slab, bytes), false, site)
    = directory
for position in 0 .. < count
    . column = table-buffer(site, tables.layouts.field(row-layout, position).layout, size)
    store(directory, position * 8, column, false, site)
= directory

────────────────────
_ do table-buffer Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - item LayoutId
    - count Operand

` A buffer of a table's storage, as TypeScript allocates one: from the task's parse region
` where one is active, and else from the collector, with what describes its items where they
` hold pointers it follows.
. row = tables.layouts.rows[item]
if row.is-managed && row.buffer == no-string
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. descriptor = if row.is-managed then buffer-descriptor else integer(.machine-pointer, 0)
    .. buffer-descriptor = make-operand(.operand-buffer-descriptor, item)
. width = integer(.machine-u64, row.size)
. region = make-operand
    - .operand-value
    - append(.op-load-task-word, site, Span(), parse-region-offset, u64-layout)
. regional = ir.reserve-block()
. collected = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-not-equal, region, integer(.machine-u64, 0)), regional, collected)
ir.start-block(collected)
. mark = pending.length
pending += width
pending += count
pending += descriptor
. made = call-runtime(.runtime-allocate-buffer, site, mark, managed-layout)
. from-heap = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(regional)
pending += width
pending += count
pending += descriptor
. carved = call-runtime(.runtime-parse-region-allocate-buffer, site, mark, managed-layout)
. from-region = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(managed-layout, carved, from-region, made, from-heap)

────────────────────
_ do fill-table
    - site SyntaxId
    - row TypeId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - columns Operand
    - size Operand
    - filler Operand

` Fills each row of a new table, from the first, with what a filler of a function type
` answers for the row's index, a call that may panic.
. counting = open-pass(site, size)
. index = counting.index
. code = load(filler, 0, pointer-layout, site)
. data = load
    - filler
    - tables.layouts.field(tables.layouts.function-layout, 1).offset
    - managed-layout
    - site
. mark = pending.length
pending += data
pending += index
. made = call(code, site, mark, .callee-value, layout-of(row, site), !in-landing)
if types.intrinsic-of(row) == .union
    scatter-union(site, tables.unions.of(row), columns, index, made, no-meta(), false, false)
else
    scatter-row(site, row-layout, columns, index, made)
close-pass(site, counting)

────────────────────
+ do table-cell Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand
    - slot U32
    - item LayoutId

` Where a row's field lies in its column: the column the directory holds for the field,
` moved on by the row's index times the size of the field.
= item-cell(site, load(columns, slot * 8, pointer-layout, site), index, item)

────────────────────
_ do item-cell Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - data Operand
    - index Operand
    - item LayoutId

` Where an item of a column lies: where the column's items start, moved on by the index times
` the size of an item.
. width = integer(.machine-u64, tables.layouts.rows[item].size)
= moved-bytes(site, data, arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-multiply, index, width, u64-layout))

────────────────────
_ do scatter-row
    - site SyntaxId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand
    - value Operand

` Stores each field of a row in its column, in the order the row declares them, through the
` collector's barrier where the field holds pointers it follows.
for position in 0 .. < tables.layouts.rows[row-layout].fields.count
    . field = tables.layouts.field(row-layout, position)
    . cell = table-cell(site, columns, index, position, field.layout)
    store-cell(site, cell, field.layout, take(value, field, site))

────────────────────
_ do store-cell
    - site SyntaxId
    - cell Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - value Operand

` Stores a value of a table's field in its cell of a table that does not grow.
. managed = tables.layouts.rows[layout].is-managed
if tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
    copy(cell, value, layout, managed, site)
else if layout != void-layout
    store(cell, 0, value, managed, site)

────────────────────
_ do gather-row Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - row-layout LayoutId
    - columns Operand
    - index Operand

` A row of a table read from its columns into the frame, field by field.
. made = frame(row-layout)
for position in 0 .. < tables.layouts.rows[row-layout].fields.count
    . field = tables.layouts.field(row-layout, position)
    . cell = table-cell(site, columns, index, position, field.layout)
    put(made, field, take(cell, LayoutField(0, field.layout, field.type), site), site)
