────────────────────
+ do table-op TableOp
    - id SyntaxId

` The operation the type pass planned at a node of a table.
. constant = facts.constant-of(unit.reading, id)
if constant == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = TableOp.table-row
= ((facts.constants[constant].bits /and/ 4294967295) as U32) as TableOp

────────────────────
_ table-slot U32
    - id SyntaxId

` The place in the row's layout of the field a table's node reads or writes.
if constant == no-fact then 0 else (facts.constants[constant].bits /rshift/ 32) as U32

.. constant = facts.constant-of(unit.reading, id)

────────────────────
_ do header-word Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - header Operand
    - position U32

` A word of the header an arena's table keeps: its columns, length, capacity, shrink and
` mutation generations, and its spill's base, use and capacity.
= load(num-cast(site, header, u64-layout, pointer-layout), position * 8, u64-layout, site)

────────────────────
_ do grows Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - header Operand

` Whether a table grows in an arena: it has a header.
= compare(site, .compare-not-equal, header, integer(.machine-u64, 0))

────────────────────
_ do view-grows Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - meta TableMeta

` Whether a view of a table reads one that grows: it has a header and an owner.
. owned = compare(site, .compare-not-equal, meta.owner, integer(.machine-u64, 0))
= bitwise(site, .bitwise-and, grows(site, meta.header), owned, u8-layout)

────────────────────
_ do header-or-zero Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - header Operand
    - position U32

` A word of a table's header where it grows, and zero where it does not.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(grows(site, header), growing, fixed)
ir.start-block(growing)
. word = header-word(site, header, position)
. from-growing = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(u64-layout, word, from-growing, integer(.machine-u64, 0), fixed)

────────────────────
_ do table-meta TableMeta
    - site SyntaxId
    - table Operand
    - layout LayoutId

` The metadata of a table value, its shrink generation read from its header where it grows.
. header = part(table, layout, 2, site)
. owner = part(table, layout, 3, site)
. incarnation = part(table, layout, 4, site)
. generation = part(table, layout, 5, site)
= TableMeta(header.operand, owner.operand, incarnation.operand, generation.operand, header-or-zero(site, header.operand, 3))

────────────────────
_ do row-meta TableMeta
    - site SyntaxId
    - row Operand
    - layout LayoutId

` The metadata a row of a table holds.
= TableMeta
    - part(row, layout, 2, site).operand
    - part(row, layout, 3, site).operand
    - part(row, layout, 4, site).operand
    - part(row, layout, 5, site).operand
    - part(row, layout, 6, site).operand

────────────────────
+ do fail-if
    - site SyntaxId
    - failed Operand
    - text String

` Raises a panic the compiler writes where a test holds. In a function that grows a table's
` storage, which raises none, the function answers the panic's message there.
. raising = ir.reserve-block()
. passed = ir.reserve-block()
branch(failed, raising, passed)
ir.start-block(raising)
if cold
    return-value(make-operand(.operand-constant, ir.add-string(text)), site)
else
    raise-text(site, text)
ir.start-block(passed)

────────────────────
_ do grow-outside
    - site SyntaxId
    - helper FunctionId
    - meta TableMeta
    - first Operand
    - second Operand
    - third Operand

` Grows a table's storage by the function the tables declared for it, given what
` `emit-storage-growth` says, and raises a panic with the message it answers where it
` answers one. A function the collector never sees leaves that zone for the call.
. target = tables.functions[helper]
. mark = pending.length
pending += meta.header
pending += meta.owner
pending += meta.incarnation
pending += first
pending += second
if operand-kind(third) != .operand-void
    pending += third
ir.depend(.callee-function, helper, 0)
. crosses = in-zone
if crosses
    cross-zone(site, false)
. message = call
    - make-operand(.operand-symbol, target.symbol)
    - site
    - mark
    - .callee-function
    - managed-layout
if crosses
    cross-zone(site, true)
. raising = ir.reserve-block()
. grown = ir.reserve-block()
branch
    - compare
        - site
        - .compare-not-equal
        - num-cast(site, message, managed-layout, u64-layout)
        - integer(.machine-u64, 0)
    - raising
    - grown
ir.start-block(raising)
raise-message(site, message)
ir.start-block(grown)

────────────────────
_ do validate-table
    - site SyntaxId
    - meta TableMeta
    - context String
    - checks-shrink Bool

` Checks that a table that grows can still be read, as TypeScript checks it: the arena has
` not been reset since, the table is not sealed, and it has not shrunk since the view was made.
` The runtime moves the generation of an arena's slot on at each reset and release and each
` time the slot is taken again, so the slot holds the generation a table was made under only
` while that arena lives unreset.
. current = load
    - num-cast(site, meta.owner, u64-layout, pointer-layout)
    - arena-generation-offset
    - u64-layout
    - site
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-not-equal, current, meta.generation)
    - "$context is stale after Arena reset"
fail-if
    - site
    - compare(site, .compare-equal, header-word(site, meta.header, 0), integer(.machine-u64, 0))
    - "Table is sealed"
if checks-shrink
    . shrunk = compare(site, .compare-not-equal, header-word(site, meta.header, 3), meta.shrink)
    fail-if(site, shrunk, "$context was invalidated by table shrink")

────────────────────
_ do table-columns Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - table Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta

` Where a table's columns are: the directory its header holds, once checked, where it grows,
` and the one it holds itself where it does not.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(grows(site, meta.header), growing, fixed)
ir.start-block(growing)
validate-table(site, meta, "Table", false)
. held = num-cast(site, header-word(site, meta.header, 0), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. from-growing = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
. own = num-cast(site, part(table, layout, 0, site).operand, managed-layout, pointer-layout)
. from-fixed = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(pointer-layout, held, from-growing, own, from-fixed)

────────────────────
_ do table-length Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - table Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta

` How many rows a table has: its header's length, once checked, where it grows, and the size
` it holds itself where it does not.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(grows(site, meta.header), growing, fixed)
ir.start-block(growing)
validate-table(site, meta, "Table", false)
. held = header-word(site, meta.header, 1)
. from-growing = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
. own = part(table, layout, 1, site)
. from-fixed = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= Typed(phi(u64-layout, held, from-growing, own.operand, from-fixed), own.type)

────────────────────
_ do table-cursor TableCursor
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - key SyntaxId

` `t[i]` of a table or of a span of one, as TypeScript reads it: the table, then the index,
` converted to one; the columns are found, and the index is checked against the length and
` moved on by the span's offset.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. empty = TableCursor(none, none, TableMeta(none, none, none, none, none))
. proven = proven-table(id)
if proven != U32.max
    . held = proven-tables[proven]
    . counted = convert(key, .reason-argument, emit-expression(key))
    if held.kind == .table || held.kind == .immutable-table
        = TableCursor(held.source.columns, counted.operand, held.source.meta)
    = TableCursor
        - held.source.columns
        - arithmetic(id, .arithmetic-add, held.source.offset, counted.operand, u64-layout)
        - held.source.meta
. table = emit-expression(object)
. type = table.type
. index = convert(key, .reason-argument, emit-expression(key))
if index.type != types.index-type || !is-row-source(intrinsic(type))
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = empty
. layout = layout-of(type, id)
= row-place(id, table.operand, type, layout, index.operand)

────────────────────
+ do rows-length Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - held Operand
    - type TypeId
    - layout LayoutId

` How many rows a table or a span of one holds, as TypeScript counts them: checked where the
` table grows, and held by a finished table and its spans.
. kind = intrinsic(type)
. length = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if kind == .table
    length = table-length(id, held, layout, table-meta(id, held, layout)).operand
else if kind == .table-span
    length = span-length(id, held, layout, span-meta(id, held, layout)).operand
else
    length = table-source(id, held, type, layout).length
= Typed(length, types.size-type)

────────────────────
+ do row-place TableCursor
    - id SyntaxId
    - table Operand
    - type TypeId
    - layout LayoutId
    - index Operand

` The row at an index of a table or of a span of one: the index checked against the length
` and moved on by the span's offset.
. kind = intrinsic(type)
. source = table-source(id, table, type, layout)
fail-if
    - id
    - compare(id, .compare-greater-equal, index, source.length)
    - "${source-name(kind)} index is out of bounds"
if kind == .table || kind == .immutable-table
    = TableCursor(source.columns, index, source.meta)
= TableCursor
    - source.columns
    - arithmetic(id, .arithmetic-add, source.offset, index, u64-layout)
    - source.meta

────────────────────
+ do table-source TableSource
    - id SyntaxId
    - table Operand
    - type TypeId
    - layout LayoutId

` The rows of a table, from the first, or of a span of one, from its offset: the columns are
` found, then the length, each checked where the table grows. A finished table and its spans
` hold their columns and length themselves, and no metadata.
. kind = intrinsic(type)
. zero = integer(.machine-u64, 0)
if kind == .immutable-table
    = TableSource
        - part-address(id, table, layout, 0).operand
        - zero
        - part(table, layout, 1, id).operand
        - TableMeta(zero, zero, zero, zero, zero)
if kind == .immutable-table-span
    = TableSource
        - part-address(id, table, layout, 0).operand
        - part(table, layout, 1, id).operand
        - part(table, layout, 2, id).operand
        - TableMeta(zero, zero, zero, zero, zero)
if kind == .table
    = table-rows(id, table, layout, table-meta(id, table, layout))
= span-rows(id, table, layout, span-meta(id, table, layout))

────────────────────
_ do table-rows TableSource
    - site SyntaxId
    - table Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta

` The columns and length of a table, from the first row: both from its header, checked once,
` where it grows, and both held by the table itself where it does not.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(grows(site, meta.header), growing, fixed)
ir.start-block(growing)
validate-table(site, meta, "Table", false)
. held = num-cast(site, header-word(site, meta.header, 0), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. held-length = header-word(site, meta.header, 1)
. from-growing = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
. own = num-cast(site, part(table, layout, 0, site).operand, managed-layout, pointer-layout)
. own-length = part(table, layout, 1, site)
. from-fixed = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
. columns = phi(pointer-layout, held, from-growing, own, from-fixed)
. length = phi(u64-layout, held-length, from-growing, own-length.operand, from-fixed)
= TableSource(columns, integer(.machine-u64, 0), length, meta)

────────────────────
_ do span-rows TableSource
    - site SyntaxId
    - span Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta

` The columns, offset and length of a span of a table, the span checked once where its table
` grows: the columns are the directory its table's header holds there, and the ones the span
` holds where it does not.
. columns = span-columns(site, span, layout, meta)
= TableSource(columns, part(span, layout, 1, site).operand, part(span, layout, 2, site).operand, meta)

────────────────────
_ do span-meta TableMeta
    - site SyntaxId
    - span Operand
    - layout LayoutId

` The metadata a span of a table holds.
= TableMeta
    - part(span, layout, 3, site).operand
    - part(span, layout, 4, site).operand
    - part(span, layout, 5, site).operand
    - part(span, layout, 6, site).operand
    - part(span, layout, 7, site).operand

────────────────────
_ do span-columns Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - span Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta

` Where a span's columns are: the directory its table's header holds, once the span is
` checked, where the table grows, and the one the span holds where it does not.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. fixed = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(view-grows(site, meta), growing, fixed)
ir.start-block(growing)
validate-table(site, meta, "TableSpan", true)
. held = num-cast(site, header-word(site, meta.header, 0), u64-layout, pointer-layout)
. from-growing = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(fixed)
. own = part-address(site, span, layout, 0)
. from-fixed = ir.current
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= phi(pointer-layout, held, from-growing, own.operand, from-fixed)

────────────────────
_ do span-length Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - span Operand
    - layout LayoutId
    - meta TableMeta

` How many rows a span of a table has, once the span is checked where its table grows.
. growing = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
branch(view-grows(site, meta), growing, joined)
ir.start-block(growing)
validate-table(site, meta, "TableSpan", true)
jump(joined)
ir.start-block(joined)
= part(span, layout, 2, site)

────────────────────
+ do emit-table-index Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - key SyntaxId

` A row of a table made a value at `t[i]`: the columns, left out where the table grows, the
` index, and the table's metadata.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if table-op(id) == TableOp.table-span
    = emit-table-span(id, object, key)
if table-op(id) == TableOp.table-item
    = emit-table-item(id, object, key)
if table-op(id) == TableOp.table-select
    = emit-table-select(id, object, key)
if table-op(id) == TableOp.span-item || table-op(id) == TableOp.selection-row
    = emit-span-index(id, object, key)
if table-op(id) == TableOp.span-range || table-op(id) == TableOp.selection-range
    = emit-span-range(id, object, key)
if table-op(id) != TableOp.table-row && table-op(id) != TableOp.proven-row
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(none, no-type)
. cursor = table-cursor(id, object, key)
= row-value(id, cursor, facts.node-type(unit.reading, id))

────────────────────
_ do emit-table-select Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - key SyntaxId

` The rows of a table indices select at `t[ids]`, as TypeScript selects them: the table, then
` the indices; a table that grows is checked, and the selection holds the table and an index
` span: the one given, or one made of the array or of the arena's builder given.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. table = emit-expression(object)
. type = table.type
. given = emit-expression(key)
. given-type = given.type
. kind = intrinsic(type)
if kind != .table && kind != .immutable-table
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(none, no-type)
. selection = facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
. layout = layout-of(type, id)
. selection-layout = layout-of(selection, id)
. span-type = field-type(selection, 1)
. span-layout = layout-of(span-type, id)
if kind == .table
    table-columns(id, table.operand, layout, table-meta(id, table.operand, layout))
. made = frame(selection-layout)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(selection-layout, 0), table.operand, id)
. span-field = tables.layouts.field(selection-layout, 1)
if given-type == span-type
    put(made, span-field, given.operand, id)
else
    span-into
        - id
        - address(made, span-field.offset, span-layout, id)
        - span-type
        - span-layout
        - given.operand
        - given-type
        - none
        - no-type
= Typed(made, selection)

────────────────────
_ do emit-span-index Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - key SyntaxId

` An index of an index span read at `s[i]`, or a row of a selection, as TypeScript reads it:
` the value, then the position, converted to one, which is checked against the length. The
` span is resolved and the index read there; a selection then reads its table's row at that
` index as `t[i]` reads it.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. held = emit-expression(object)
. type = held.type
. position = convert(key, .reason-argument, emit-expression(key))
if position.type != types.index-type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, key)
    = Typed(none, no-type)
. layout = layout-of(type, id)
if intrinsic(type) == .index-span
    . item = viewed-item(type)
    . item-layout = layout-of(item, id)
    fail-if
        - id
        - compare(id, .compare-greater-equal, position.operand, word-at(id, held.operand, layout, 3))
        - "IndexSpan index is out of bounds"
    . value = span-item(id, resolve-span(id, held.operand, layout), position.operand, item-layout)
    = Typed(value, item)
= row-value(id, selected-row(id, held.operand, type, layout, position.operand), facts.node-type(unit.reading, id))

────────────────────
_ do selection-cursor TableCursor
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - key SyntaxId

` The row a selection reads at `s[i]`, where a field of it is read or written: the selection,
` then the position, converted to one.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. empty = TableCursor(none, none, TableMeta(none, none, none, none, none))
. held = emit-expression(object)
. type = held.type
. position = convert(key, .reason-argument, emit-expression(key))
. kind = intrinsic(type)
if position.type != types.index-type || not-selection
